                    text: "Three auditors flagged gaps in the electronic edit logs (audit trails) that companies must keep. At **Campus**, new accounting software had no independent controls report, so the auditor could not say whether its database log was switched on, could not comment on possible tampering from April to December 2025, and said the audit trail ‘has not been preserved’ as required. At **Wakefit**, the revenue software had no edit log, and the auditor could not confirm database-level logging for its ledger software. At **Honasa**, one price-master application ran without an edit log all year, and three systems do not log changes by privileged users. **Mayur**'s auditor made the ₹102.7cr polyurethane plant, which made operating losses in both FY25 and FY26, a key audit matter, relying on an outside valuer. **Sheela Foam**'s key audit matter is ₹1,612cr of goodwill and brands. No qualified audit opinion was found in the group. **Bajaj Consumer**'s auditor, by contrast, confirmed that its SAP edit log ran all year and was preserved; its only key audit matter is the estimate of trade discounts and rebates, and contingent liabilities are just ₹9.9cr of indirect-tax claims. **My view: missing edit logs are not evidence of wrongdoing, but together with CFO exits at Campus and Wakefit they argue for smaller positions.**",
